    topic: "free-help", phrase: "finding free business help and mentoring", us: true,
    steps: [
      S("Learn what free help is out there", "In the United States, the SBA and its partners offer free or low-cost counselling and training. The partners are Small Business Development Centers, SCORE business mentors, Women's Business Centers and Veterans Business Outreach Centers. Knowing the names helps you ask for the right one.", ["Nothing yet, just listen"], "localAssistance", "you can name at least two of the four kinds of free or low-cost help.", [W("SBA", "the Small Business Administration, the United States government agency that helps small businesses."), W("SBDC", "Small Business Development Center: a local office that gives small business owners free or low-cost counselling and training."), W("SCORE", "a group of business mentors who give free advice to small business owners.")]),
      S("Find the office near you", "Go to the SBA local assistance page and search by your ZIP code. It lists the offices near you. I cannot look up addresses myself, so the search page is the place to do it. Write down the name, the phone number and the hours of the one you choose.", ["Your ZIP code", "The SBA local assistance page open", "A pen and paper"], "localAssistance", "you have the name and phone number of one office near you written down.", [W("ZIP code", "the five-digit number the post office gives each area, used here to find help near you.")]),
      S("Ask for a free SCORE mentor", "SCORE mentoring is free. You request a mentor on the SCORE website, and you do not need a business plan or an established business first. Expect a reply within about two days. The guide does not say what to do if you hear nothing after that, so contact a SCORE chapter or the SBA office near you.", ["The SCORE website open", "An email address or phone number where you can be reached"], "scoreFaq", "you have sent your request for a mentor, or you know exactly why you chose not to yet.", [W("Mentor", "an experienced person who gives you advice and guidance.")]),
      S("Get your questions ready", OWN + "Before your first meeting, write down three things: what your business is or will be, what you need help with most, and your questions. The guide says counselors can help you prepare your plan and records and find the licenses you need, so bring what you have, even if it is only an idea.", ["A pen and paper", "Any papers about your business, even rough notes"], null, "you have a page with what your business is, what you need most, and at least three questions.", []),
      S("Know about the MBDA centers", "The Minority Business Development Agency has funded Business Centers for minority-owned businesses, but the guide could not confirm which are open today. Contact a center to confirm before you rely on it. The guide says SBDCs, SCORE mentors and Women's Business Centers are the dependable free help, so start there.", ["The SBA local assistance page open"], "localAssistance", "you know that an MBDA center must be confirmed open before you rely on it, and that SBDCs and SCORE are the dependable choice.", [W("MBDA", "the Minority Business Development Agency, a federal agency that has funded centers for minority-owned businesses.")])
    ]
